{
    "background_story": "Jaxon was a struggling artist, working multiple jobs to make ends meet while pursuing his passion for theater. He stumbled upon an obscure play, 'Thespis,' which told the story of the ancient Greek actor who defied tradition by speaking lines instead of reciting them. Inspired by Thespis' courage, Jaxon decided to stage his own production of the play. Despite the initial skepticism from his peers, Jaxon's innovative direction and passionate performance brought the story to life. The play became a surprise hit, earning Jaxon critical acclaim and recognition within the theater community. His success was not just a testament to his talent but also to the power of taking risks and challenging conventional norms, just like the ancient thespian who dared to be different.",
